<title>GERMANY: Rheinmetall seeks Kolbenschmidt majority.</title>
<headline>Rheinmetall seeks Kolbenschmidt majority.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany defence and engineering group Rheinmetall AG said it would be seeking to secure a majority stake in car components manufacturer Kolbenschmidt AG this year.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Rheinmetall in Duesseldorf confirmed in response to enquiries that this was its intention. Earlier, Rheinmetall said it had an agreement to take over a 24.99 percent stake in Kolbenschmidt from Commerzbank AG.</p>
<p>He gave no further details of how it would achieve this.</p>
<p>Britain's T&amp;N Plc has options over a further, similar-sized stake which is currently parked with institutional investors and once also belonged to Commerzbank.</p>
<p>German bank Metallbank, which acquired the stake from Commerzbank last December, has the right to recall the stake if required.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
